  "site_name": "Inner Temple Treasury",
  "description": "Tree Maintenance Works\rTree 60 - London plane in main car park \rSurvey comment - No Massaria evident at inspection. Root plate lifting adjacent tarmac beyond tree pit. Used for car Parking. Recommended to reduce outer eastern portion of canopy by approximately 2m to suitable growth points to allow T82 space to grow\r- Sensitively reduce longer protruding elements of the outer eastern canopy from adjacent trees, by 2m, maintaining natural flowing lines and shape and form. \r- All cuts to be made back to suitable secondary growth points \r\rTree 72 - Magnolia spp. in Master's House Garden\rSurvey comment - Eastern canopy growing close to adjacent building \r- Sensitively reduce growth towards building by 1m, maintaining natural flowing lines and shape and form. \r- All cuts to be made back to suitable secondary growth points \r\rTree group refs 76, 77, 78 and 79 - 4 x Betula utilis 'Jacquemontii' (Himalayan birch) in Hare Court Courtyard \rSurvey comment - Trees are growing in close proximity to each other and suppressing trees beneath, some have broken and suspended branches \r- (With consent from CoL Tree Officer) - Carry out sensitive and selective branch reduction works by approx. 1.5-2m using 'drop crotch' pruning techniques to alleviate weight loading on heavy end weighted branches which are dropping down, some of which have snapped out \r- Remove hangers / broken and suspended branches  \r- Remove crowded and crossing branches\r\rTree group refs 80, 81 and 82 - 3 x Liquidambar styraciflua (Sweet gum) in car park planted beds\rSurvey comment - Lower canopy growth is encroaching into walkways\r- Crown lift to 2.5m to an even level to provide adequate clearance over footpath",
